hanged the error message to `gin: response body already written`. The `errHijackAlreadyWritten` name stays the same, so anyone comparing against that error is unaffected.\n- I added a test case to `response_writer_test.go` for hijacking after only the header has been sent. `go test ./...` passes.\n\nI haven't committed anything, because you're on a detached HEAD. I can create a branch and commit it as `fix(response): refine hijack behavior for response lifecycle` if you want. One thing to know: handlers that relied on the old error when hijacking after only headers were flushed will now hijack successfully instead.","ttft_ms":4193,"type":"result","duration_ms":27329,"uuid":"257fac30-95df-49e0-b4ff-6df9ea2e4e5a","ttft_stream_ms":1037,"time_to_request_ms":369,"first_content_frame_ms":1038,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
